        "anchor_id": "best-deck-for-rv",
        "heading": "What's the Best Deck for an RV or Camper?",
        "answer": "For a seasonal or long stay site, the best deck for an RV is a floating deck on its own footings, sized to the door side of your rig. It feels like a real deck, never puts load on the RV, and keeps the trailer free to move. Portable fold out platforms suit travelers who change campsites every few days.",
        "text": "Your seasonal site is where mornings start slow and evenings run long. It deserves more than a mat on the grass. Every A-DIY kit is a professionally engineered deck system: the structure is designed in advance, the parts arrive ready to assemble, and the footings and hardware come in the box.",
        "image_alt": "Two dogs relaxing on an A-DIY wood deck outside a camper",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/rv-deck-camper-dogs.png"
      }
